#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:10
msgid ""
"The [full topic synthesis](ledger-invoices-and-registers.md) covers "
"bank/manual ledger entries, classification and readiness, invoice "
"catalogue intake and reciprocal linking, document evidence and reviewed "
"confirmation, LLM proposals, and the local IVA prorrata register. A "
"parser-supported document first becomes lower-confidence evidence/draft; "
"re-extraction and per-finding human review precede canonical invoice "
"creation. Calculation readiness screens classified rows and links, while "
"finalized calculation references block fact changes. These are local "
"financial source capabilities, not official exports or remote filings. "
"Ledger guards (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_common.py`) "
"Invoice intake (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/bulk_import.py`) "
"Confirmation (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) "
"([049](../articles/049-invoice-intake-catalogue-lifecycle-and-operation-"
"boundaries.md), [051](../articles/051-ledger-classification-import-"
"export-and-lifecycle-services.md), [052](../articles/052-manual-ledger-"
"services-evidence-operations-and-batch-ingestion.md), "
"[053](../articles/053-iva-classification-assembly-confirmation-checks-"
"and-readiness.md), [057](../articles/057-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-"
"reviewed-confirmation.md), [060](../articles/060-ledger-contracts-"
"attribution-readiness-and-ratios.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:12
msgid ""
"Enforced controls include exact-profile operation access, revision-"
"guarded ledger/event and invoice/transaction writes, content-derived "
"evidence identity, explicit missing/ambiguous document facts, and "
"canonical consent for off-host extraction: the registered path requires "
"stored evidence, per-call acknowledgement, a minted source-hash proof and"
" a loaded-byte digest check. Model classification remains a proposal; "
"registry rules derive tax amounts and a captured reviewed baseline gates "
"application. The prorrata seed rechecks prior M303 revision and commits "
"against source plus register revisions. Consent path "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_extract_operation.py`) "
"Reviewed LLM apply "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/llm_review_execution.py`) Prorrata seed "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/prorrata_register/service.py`) "
"([054](../articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-"
"evidence-provenance.md), [055](../articles/055-evidence-custody-review-"
"and-ingestion-operations.md), [058](../articles/058-deterministic-"
"invoice-labels-and-core-ledger-surfaces.md), [059](../articles/059-llm-"
"ledger-review-diagnostics-and-merge.md), [061](../articles/061-ledger-"
"operations-rule-application-and-filing-readiness.md), "
"[062](../articles/062-ledger-workspace-projection-and-read-"
"boundaries.md), [095](../articles/095-profile-scoped-iva-prorrata-"
"register-operations.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:14
msgid ""
"The key cross-layer question is whether a draft tax ID without its own "
"accepted anchor can be promoted by separate role text and later accepted;"
" model output, deterministic grounding and human confirmation must remain"
" distinct. Confirmation's catalogue, attachment, evidence-summary and "
"audit writes are sequential, so crash recovery needs verification. Ratio "
"override and event writes are explicitly non-atomic; importer original-"
"file hashing is separately timed. An IRPF-residency proxy can over-report"
" issuer IVA establishment in non-TAI territories. Identity seam "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/grounded_reading.py`) Confirmation "
"writes (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) Ratio "
"ordering (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/ratios.py`) "
"([050](../articles/050-invoice-profile-advisories-source-mesh-resolution-"
"and-linking.md), [056](../articles/056-document-grounding-evidence-"
"routing-history-and-import-export.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:20
msgid ""
"The ledger is the local transaction authority for imports, manual "
"entries, classifications, evidence links, and calculation participation. "
"An invoice catalogue represents issued and received invoices separately, "
"and a reciprocal link joins an invoice to a transaction. Purchase-"
"evidence records are a lower-confidence layer around stored document "
"bytes; an extraction draft proposes facts; human confirmation can create "
"a canonical invoice. This hierarchy matters: a parsable document, a model"
" suggestion, a confirmed invoice, and a tax-ready ledger row carry "
"different claims. The application also maintains an IVA prorrata register"
" for cross-period calculation inputs. Ledger action ports "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/action_ports.py`) Evidence record "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/evidence.py`) Invoice writer "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/catalogue_creation.py`) Prorrata "
"service (`src/cadrumo/application/prorrata_register/service.py`) "
"([049](../articles/049-invoice-intake-catalogue-lifecycle-and-operation-"
"boundaries.md), [051](../articles/051-ledger-classification-import-"
"export-and-lifecycle-services.md), [055](../articles/055-evidence-"
"custody-review-and-ingestion-operations.md), [095](../articles/095"
"-profile-scoped-iva-prorrata-register-operations.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:22
msgid "Import, lifecycle, and calculation readiness"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:24
msgid ""
"Ledger import stages CSV, OFX/QFX, XLS/XLSX and named provider inputs "
"through injected adapters. It checks source/provider, parses and "
"classifies rows with the same evaluator used by dry-run diagnostics, then"
" saves accepted transactions and events under revision guards. Stored "
"direction/currency-qualified fingerprints skip known rows; repeated same-"
"signature movements in one statement can remain distinct when IDs differ."
" An unresolved FX conversion remains visibly absent rather than using a "
"foreign face amount as euros. Directory planning is deterministic, and "
"bulk work reports partial outcomes. The staged rows do not change if the "
"source path later changes, although the separately reopened original-file"
" hash may then describe different bytes. Diagnostic events are appended "
"after the primary import co-commit, so a later diagnostic failure can "
"follow already durable rows. Import staging "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_import.py`) Deduplication "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_import.py`) Co-commit and "
"diagnostics (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_import.py`) "
"([051](../articles/051-ledger-classification-import-export-and-lifecycle-"
"services.md), [052](../articles/052-manual-ledger-services-evidence-"
"operations-and-batch-ingestion.md), [056](../articles/056-document-"
"grounding-evidence-routing-history-and-import-export.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:26
msgid ""
"Manual add and edit validate dated registry categories, "
"invoice/evidence/usage references and canonical amounts. Idempotency keys"
" make identical adds no-ops and reject changed payloads under the same "
"key. Classification rules support inspectable plans and per-row apply; "
"bulk CSV classification preserves omitted fields. Lifecycle actions "
"archive, stash, restore, mark reviewed-excluded, remove or reset, with "
"dry-run for destructive cases. A finalized calculation reference blocks "
"fact changes or removal; draft references become stale advisories. "
"Split/merge preserve monetary totals, archive lineage and use revision-"
"guarded writes. Source-backed actor strings are audit labels, not "
"identity proof; exact-profile registered operations supply authorization."
" Some follow-on attachment manifest updates occur after transaction/event"
" commit and can leave an incomplete backlink if they fail; operations "
"report unknown or partial effect rather than a false no-op. Manual "
"mutation (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_manual.py`) Finalized "
"guard (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_common.py`) Split/merge "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/actions_split_merge.py`) Rule effect "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/rule_operation.py`) "
"([051](../articles/051-ledger-classification-import-export-and-lifecycle-"
"services.md), [052](../articles/052-manual-ledger-services-evidence-"
"operations-and-batch-ingestion.md), [061](../articles/061-ledger-"
"operations-rule-application-and-filing-readiness.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:28
msgid ""
"Readiness is a separate read-only analysis. It screens active rows by "
"filing date for classification, IVA and EUR substrate, counterparty "
"identity/establishment, deduction, home-office censo and non-declarable "
"categories, and checks reciprocal invoice links. The IVA issue taxonomy "
"has an exhaustive mapping to reachable preflight checks or explicit non-"
"reachability. Ledger workspace and list/review/detail projections retain "
"financial facts needed by an authorized operator, distinguish unmeasured "
"queues from empty ones, and surface stale declarations and link "
"inconsistencies. Ratio overrides are year-sensitive and can derive a "
"home-office share from censo, but profile state and the audit event are "
"separate writes; an event failure can leave a changed ratio without its "
"event. Preflight (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/preflight.py`) Link "
"check (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/check_query.py`) Workspace "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/workspace.py`) Ratio ordering "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/ratios.py`) ([053](../articles/053-iva-"
"classification-assembly-confirmation-checks-and-readiness.md), "
"[060](../articles/060-ledger-contracts-attribution-readiness-and-"
"ratios.md), [061](../articles/061-ledger-operations-rule-application-and-"
"filing-readiness.md), [062](../articles/062-ledger-workspace-projection-"
"and-read-boundaries.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:30
msgid "Invoice and document pathway"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:32
msgid ""
"Invoice bulk intake supports CSV/TSV/XLS/XLSX/XLSM, rejects formula "
"cells, uses exact canonical/alias headers before an optional semantic "
"mapper, requires country evidence per row, and processes acceptable rows "
"one by one through the same canonical writer as manual add. Structured "
"single invoices can have multiple ordered IVA lines; file imports have "
"one rate per row. Dated registry facts validate rates and categories; "
"accepted invoices get a content-addressed ID and catalogue/event co-"
"commit. List/view/update/remove use exact-profile operations. Invoice "
"deletion refuses linked transactions; updates preserve identity and "
"links, while bidirectional linking commits both catalogues with revision "
"witnesses. The source resolver provides collectible/payable and M347/M349"
" values, withholding unconverted FX or ambiguous/contradictory "
"declaration classifications with diagnostics. M347/M349 operator "
"aggregation remains a preview distinct from this live source mesh. Bulk "
"intake (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/bulk_import.py`) Canonical "
"create (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/catalogue_creation.py`) Atomic "
"link (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/transaction_linking.py`) Invoice "
"source (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/source_resolver.py`) "
"([049](../articles/049-invoice-intake-catalogue-lifecycle-and-operation-"
"boundaries.md), [050](../articles/050-invoice-profile-advisories-source-"
"mesh-resolution-and-linking.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:34
msgid ""
"Evidence custody hashes and probes files before deriving draft identity. "
"PDF text layers use deterministic labels first, then semantic fill only "
"where incomplete; scans/images take a vision route, while structured "
"Facturae/CII/UBL use exact readers. Unknown XML refuses. Model-"
"unavailable paths can retain a partial deterministic draft; no model "
"output is itself a confirmed invoice. Decrypted bytes and transcriptions "
"have in-process no-serialization tripwires, and source paths are not "
"fallback byte sources. The canonical off-host extraction operation "
"requires a stored evidence ID, explicit acknowledgement, a proof minted "
"for provider and source hash, and a check that loaded bytes match the "
"token address before dispatch. This is the enforced canonical consent "
"path; a generic lower-level caller's weaker contract alone does not prove"
" a reachable bypass. Evidence input "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/evidence_input.py`) Extraction routing "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_draft_extraction.py`) Consent "
"mint and byte check "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_evidence_extract_operation.py`) "
"([055](../articles/055-evidence-custody-review-and-ingestion-"
"operations.md), [056](../articles/056-document-grounding-evidence-"
"routing-history-and-import-export.md), [057](../articles/057-invoice-"
"evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:36
msgid ""
"Grounding compares proposed values with independent transcription "
"anchors, using token boundaries and numeric parsing, but a text match "
"does not prove semantic role. Party colocation and identity checks add "
"independent role evidence. A specific draft path may promote an "
"originally unanchored tax ID when role text is accepted and an absent "
"printed anchor falls back to the candidate value; later blockers and "
"human confirmation must be traced before calling that accepted ledger "
"identity. Human confirmation re-extracts bytes, checks source and review "
"digests, demands per-finding answers, records operator corrections as "
"unanchored operator assertions, and delegates invoice creation to the "
"canonical writer. It then links attachment, updates evidence summary and "
"writes a confirmation record in separate steps, so a crash can interrupt "
"the provenance chain despite an operation-level unknown-effect report. "
"Grounding (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/grounding_anchor.py`) Identity"
" candidate seam (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/grounded_reading.py`) "
"Review gate (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/confirmation_gate.py`) "
"Confirmation persistence "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_confirmation.py`) "
"([054](../articles/054-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-"
"evidence-provenance.md), [056](../articles/056-document-grounding-"
"evidence-routing-history-and-import-export.md), [057](../articles/057"
"-invoice-evidence-extraction-and-reviewed-confirmation.md), "
"[058](../articles/058-deterministic-invoice-labels-and-core-ledger-"
"surfaces.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:38
msgid ""
"Territorial classification distinguishes counterparty establishment from "
"VAT registration and document evidence from remembered operator "
"assertions. Missing country or Spanish postal evidence does not silently "
"become mainland Spain. The issuer-establishment advisory uses an IRPF "
"residency proxy that is explicitly over-strict for territories outside "
"the Spanish IVA area; it is advisory rather than a filing gate. "
"Deterministic label parsing handles finite Spanish/Catalan/English "
"vocabulary and keeps ambiguous thousand/decimal readings unresolved. "
"Printed IVA/total checks are advisories and do not overwrite derived "
"figures. Establishment ladder "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/establishment_ladder.py`) Classifier "
"facts (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/classification_assembly.py`) Proxy"
" limit (`src/cadrumo/application/invoices/issuer_establishment.py`) Label"
" parsing "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/invoice_label_value_parsing.py`) "
"([050](../articles/050-invoice-profile-advisories-source-mesh-resolution-"
"and-linking.md), [053](../articles/053-iva-classification-assembly-"
"confirmation-checks-and-readiness.md), [054](../articles/054"
"-confirmation-gate-counterparty-establishment-and-evidence-"
"provenance.md), [058](../articles/058-deterministic-invoice-labels-and-"
"core-ledger-surfaces.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:40
msgid ""
"LLM classification is a reviewed proposal path. The model may suggest "
"business/category or split proportions; pinned registry calculation "
"derives IVA base, rate and quota, and canonical writers apply accepted "
"facts under a captured transaction baseline. A continuation verifies "
"invocation, digest and authority generation before commit. Rejection "
"records an event without changing the row. Ordinary review defaults "
"evidence reading off, and a MIXED percentage can fall back to the model "
"suggestion; the UI acceptance and evidence policy need cross-layer "
"verification. Diagnostics report usage/cost and current stamped "
"confidence without response text, though date filters apply to usage and "
"not confidence. Suggestion and tax derivation "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/llm_classification.py`) Review "
"continuation (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/llm_review_execution.py`) "
"Diagnostics (`src/cadrumo/application/ledger/llm_diagnostics.py`) "
"([059](../articles/059-llm-ledger-review-diagnostics-and-merge.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:42
msgid "Prorrata register and quality boundary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:44
msgid ""
"The profile prorrata register supports sector declaration, "
"general/especial election, revocation, provisional seeding and definitive"
" settlement. Whole-entity seed selects a prior M303 settlement under the "
"pinned authority, re-confirms its stamped revision and coordinates, then "
"commits against both source and register revisions. Sector carry uses "
"that sector's own prior definitive entry. These are local register "
"mutations feeding calculations, not AEAT filing. The seed reader's "
"official-source and taxpayer scope depend on its repository snapshot "
"port, a specific adapter check still needed. Seed selection "
"(`src/cadrumo/application/prorrata_register/seed.py`) Source-fenced "
"commit (`src/cadrumo/application/prorrata_register/service.py`) Sector "
"carry (`src/cadrumo/application/prorrata_register/sector_lifecycle.py`) "
"([095](../articles/095-profile-scoped-iva-prorrata-register-"
"operations.md))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../technical/topics/ledger-invoices-and-registers.md:46
msgid ""
"The strongest controls across this family are exact bucket binding, "
"revision guards, co-commit where a shared store supports it, content "
"identity, explicit missing evidence, and human review before model-"
"derived facts become canonical. Remaining checks should target "
"confirmation multi-store recovery, the unanchored identity seam, "
"ratio/event split, import hash timing, adapter consent audit, and whether"
" weaker inferred classification states are presented to operators. Static"
" inspection did not execute readers, stores, models or filing paths and "
"does not validate bundled legal rules."
msgstr ""

